258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (For this issue, we are diving into a tech-nological and digital world to examine how technology can help and hinder art prod-uction. We ourselves are a digital magazine, and benefit immensely from the low costs associated with running this type of pub-lication. We connect with our readers and contributors on social media, share our mag-azine on the internet, and can see that much of the Irish creative community is bolstered by an online presence. However, technology can also be seen to have a negative impact on the creation of artwork, and existing in online spaces is far from free of engaging with commercial incentives. Advertisers, algo-rithms and artificial intelligence have ren-dered the internet a precarious space for artists to exist within. It is with these con-flicting ideas in mind that we set this issue topic.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (A couple of key themes can be seen to emerge throughout the pieces you will read in this issue. Perhaps unsurprisingly, artificial intel-ligence is brought up again and again as an area of key concern. Anya Wilson discusses how AI makes it easier for online companies )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
