/E (I stalled. He was pointing directly at me, leading her gaze to my one, black eye. For the first time, she was seeing me. I scrambled to whiz politely, inclining downwards in a nervous, mock nod, but the movement was too slight for her to see. That shock turned to a frown. 87% disgust, 6% fear, 7% disappointment. I flashed red in a steady rhythm in some desperate attempt to show her that I was alive. That I was watching. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (Her eyes rolled back to the man at her side, who was already busy fumbling with something in his pocket. Palm-sized, rough and jagged at the edges, tossed twice to demonstrate the weight, placed into the centre of her hand with a pleased smile. She thumbed it. A chunk of concrete, from the con-struction site on Parlour Road.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (One step into the street, and I could feel my systems heating up. We were holding eye contact now, as she stalked across the road. Knuckles white around the concrete. I am so much taller than her, so much more powerful than she could ever be. Her arm reeled back. Even twisted in anger, even roaring with frustration, she was beautiful. The con-crete flew from her fingertips, and my glass shattered.  )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
