/E (Despite the very different tech-nological conditions facing hu-mans then and now, the writing still resonates in a number of ways and is very much worth reading. When I first encoun-tered it last year, it bridged a large gap in my thinking)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (between women and machines. I began to think of myself more as a cyborg, and it noticeably shifted how I perceived and engaged with my smartphone, as one example. Reading the essay shifted something funda-mental in me: it challenged the idea that I was a slave to technology and replaced it with a more autonomous unders-tanding. I started to see that access to technology, under cer-tain conditions, makes me stronger than human.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
