/Title (Still, frazzled and rushing, she was beautiful. The planes of her face were soft, yet perfectly defined when kissed by sunlight. Photogenic in the way that she was almost always caught smiling and when she wasn't there was hardly an angle that disagreed with her. I watched as she picked up the pace down the street with a hand wrapped around a mug, glasses on her forehead, and keys jingling wildly on her wrist. I watched and watched and she disappeared around the corner. Not to return until 6:13PM, after her commute home, or 8:37PM, if she went to a barre class after work.)
